From 13bfd3c293349f514a908bcf2a9fd5dcc41296f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:07:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve V8 Python generators across execution platforms

Focused Windows generator analysis fails on the Linux baseline with no matching wheel; hosted Windows cross builds fail for the inverse host mismatch. Resolve native, Linux and Windows wheels, and update only the required MarkupSafe pin to 3.0.4 to avoid its failing Python 3.11 source fallback. Keep Jinja2 and hash checks unchanged.

Inspector generation also reproduces missing imports from hardcoded repository paths. Use the explicit supported zipapp launcher while retaining manifest runfiles. Both platform analyses and actual inspector generation pass through tools/build-warnings/v8/check-python-platforms.sh. Fresh emitted-patch formatting and lock verification follow in the owning repair goal.

Consolidate follow-up corrections while preserving the final implementation:
- zzz-v8-inspector-python-runtime.patch
- zzz-v8-python-execution-platforms.patch

Original focused red/green records remain in the owning task evidence.
Fresh emitted-queue verification is a separate acceptance gate.
---
